  ('4270978c-a208-4d6b-8e6c-efd130ad45c2'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000306'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99424', 'covered', '{"answer":"Ohio Medicaid''s Appendix DD to rule 5160-1-60, revised 01/01/2026, does not list 99424 (principal care management, first 30 minutes by a physician or other qualified health professional) on any of its 8 tabs. It is absent, not denied: of the 9,617 distinct codes the workbook carries, the two either side of it are consecutive — 99423 (Ol dig e/m svc 21+ min) followed directly by 99429 (Unlisted preventive medicine service) — with no row in between. The schedule''s blanket exclusion note denies unlisted codes only within the ranges it enumerates, and every one of those ranges is a letter series (G, P, S, T, W, X, Y, Z) — no 99xxx range appears among them. So Ohio publishes neither a rate nor a coverage designation for this code, and Buckeye Health Plan has no state determination to follow. Confirm with the plan before billing.","source":"Ohio Medicaid Appendix DD to rule 5160-1-60, revised 01/01/2026, read 2026-08-12","rateBasis":null,"stateFfsRate":null}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.7, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'c83c573f-ef17-4117-8ede-8e141a4b1431'::uuid, 'Appendix DD to rule 5160-1-60 (Non-Institutional Fee Schedule), revised 01/01/2026 — 99423 | 99429', 'extract:oh-carecoord-absent-2026-08'),
